<!--
    A dedicated channel for the AI extraction jobs.

    The source module did not ship this record, on the grounds that queue_job
    stores the channel as a plain string and auto-creates the node. True, but
    every other module in THIS tree that enqueues work declares its channel
    (`goodahead_claude` -> claude_api, `goodahead_fraud_detection` ->
    fraud_detection, trackpod -> two, twilio_transport, the three conversion
    modules), so the record is here to match the convention and, more usefully,
    so the channel shows up in the UI where its capacity can be set.

    🔴 It is NOT `root.claude_api`, even though these are Claude calls.
    `goodahead_fraud_detection` already keeps its own channel rather than
    sharing that one, and for a good reason: an AI invoice extraction takes
    ~60 s and may queue in bulk when somebody uploads a folder of PDFs. Sharing
    a channel would let a batch of invoices starve fraud detection, which is
    latency-sensitive in a way this is not.

    ⚠️ Capacity is a DEPLOY-CONFIG setting, not a field on this record — the
    `channels = root:N,root.ai_import:1` line in odoo.conf. Without it the
    channel inherits root's capacity and the point of having it is lost.
-->
<odoo noupdate="1">
    <record id="channel_ai_import" model="queue.job.channel">
        <field name="name">ai_import</field>
        <field name="parent_id" ref="queue_job.channel_root"/>
    </record>
</odoo>
